<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3624" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ărĭĕtīnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		aries. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>from a ram</i>, <i>ram's-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ungula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					29, 4, 27, § 88</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulmo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					30, 8, 22, § 72</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 4, 10, 28</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Similar to a ram's head</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cicer,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 10, 20</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 12, 32, § 124</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Petr.
			35</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			Arietinum oraculum,
			<i>an ambiguous oracle</i> (the figure taken from the
			divergent horns of a ram), <i><span class="en">Gell. 3, 3, 8</span></i> (cf.
					<i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. A. 4,
		196</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
